    You enjoy the rest of the film, occasionally turning back to the brothers. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> naps peacefully the rest of the show as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> continues to watch with a smirk that he just can’t hide. It is clear he is enjoying the movie a lot.  <br>
    <br>
    As it ends and the theater begins to empty, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> picks up his sleeping brother and carries him outside alongside you. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“That was pretty good.”</span> He says, trying not to sound too excited, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> has a hard time staying awake during movies, but I’m sure he enjoyed it. Though, guess I should get him home. Once he’s out, he’s not coming back for a few hours.”</span> <span style="color:lightgreen">You smile and say goodbye to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span>, happy you got to spend time with both of them.</span>  <br>
